        "text": "There is a human trial, and it is worth being precise about what it showed. [A 2021 study in Nutrients](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8227740/) gave 236 overweight adults either the Hafnia alvei probiotic or a placebo for twelve weeks. Both groups were also put on a 20% calorie deficit with standardised counselling. More people in the probiotic group reached the 3% weight-loss mark — 54.9% against 41.4%, p = 0.048. That is a real randomised result and I am not going to dismiss it. It is also a proof-of-concept study, with a p-value sitting right on the line, in which everybody was dieting. It is not evidence that a bacterium is running your appetite."
